        "headline": "Meet The Practitioner",
        "large_headline": "Daniel Rahmann",
        "copy": "<p>As a registered dietitian nutritionist, health coach, and QoL Strategic Director, Daniel collaborates closely with Dr. Christie to integrate nutrition therapy and longevity science into personalized strategies that optimize health, enhance cellular function, and reverse biological aging.</p><p>Daniel’s expertise is grounded in his training at the USC Leonard Davis School of Gerontology, where he conducted research on the fasting-mimicking diet and contributed to clinical trials exploring its therapeutic application in breast cancer and autoimmune diseases through the Longo Lab and Create Cures Foundation. His clinical rotations in oncology, across both inpatient and outpatient settings informs his ability to address complex, nutrition-related health challenges with precision and compassion.</p><p>Through data-driven, patient-centered strategies, Daniel develops targeted protocols involving advanced supplementation, therapeutic nutrition, and lifestyle optimization. As your health evolves, he works alongside you to refine, monitor, and adapt your plan, ensuring lasting alignment with Dr. Christie’s comprehensive, globally informed approach to healthy aging.</p>",
